Z||000000||Kage86GT4SP||07-13-99||01:08 AM||||The TPS!!!<p>I replaced it today, and noticed an immediate difference... with the old one, the car would start at 3200 RPM and gradually drop to 1800...<p>I replaced it, hit the key, and the engine RPM at start dropped from 3200 to 2500, an immediate reduction of 700 RPM at start up.<p>Within 2 minutes, the idle dropped to 900 RPM...<p>Problem solved!<p>My thanks to everyone who responded, but especially to theogre, who hit (if you'll pardon the expression) the nail on the head!<p>When I opened the sensor up to see what was up, the two curved, circular metal strips that the contacts touch when the lever was pressed as the throttle was pressed had completely worn away.<p>Minor detail, heh?<p>Thanks again, all!<br>K
